00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.620
Joe: First let’s start with
some broad strokes on Autism.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.760
Autism spectrum disorder covers a wide
variation of symptoms and the severity of

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.500
those symptoms that can be experienced.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.910
It can occur in all
ethnic and racial groups.

00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:48.890
It is estimated that there are
around 700,000 people in the UK,

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:52.660
including one in 100 children,
diagnosed with autism spectrum

00:00:52.660 --> 00:01:12.690
disorder according to the BMA in 2020.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:13.027
Beth: Autism spectrum disorder is
a lifelong developmental condition,

00:01:13.027 --> 00:01:13.616
related to brain development and affects
the way a child, young person or adult

00:01:13.616 --> 00:01:14.122
responds to the world around them
and impacts how they perceive others.

00:01:14.122 --> 00:01:14.543
Joe: On the whole individuals with
autism have untypical social interactions

00:01:14.543 --> 00:01:17.840
or communication and may have some
restrictive and or repetitive behaviours.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:22.390
However, the characteristics of autism
can vary so much from individual

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.670
to individual, especially depending
on where they are on the spectrum.

00:01:26.349 --> 00:01:29.780
Beth: The way autism spectrum disorder
affects children and young people

00:01:30.029 --> 00:01:34.360
can also change as they grow, develop
and experience different environments

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.850
and move through life’s major phases.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.809
But they will, depending on where
they are on the spectrum, always need

00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:44.619
some form of support to help them
throughout their life, especially

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:48.540
as they try to gain employment or
live independently within society.

00:01:49.059 --> 00:01:53.070
Joe: So, we can see that although it
is a lifelong condition, there are

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.660
treatments and services that can help
to improve an individual’s symptoms

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.320
and ability to function better.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.479
Special education and support
programmes can also help improve

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.779
their chances so that individuals
can reach their full potential and

00:02:05.779 --> 00:02:07.729
secure the highest quality of life.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:12.045
Beth: So let’s start to look a little
more into the condition of Autism and

00:02:12.045 --> 00:02:13.370
work to increase our understanding.

